{"text": "Category A is Physically Dependent. The educational description is: A student who is completely dependent on others for all major daily living needs and requires continuous assistance for feeding, dressing, toileting, mobility, and personal hygiene in order to attend school. This description is about educational impact and the support required for meaningful participation. It should not be used as a prediction of intelligence, personality, or future potential.\n\nOur fictional student is Olivia Chen, who is in Grade 6 and uses she/her pronouns. Olivia has spinal muscular atrophy. She uses a power wheelchair, needs full personal-care support, and has age-appropriate reasoning and academic understanding. This background information matters because it connects the designation to observable access needs at school.\n\nWhen we plan for Olivia, we ask three practical questions: What can the student already do? What barriers are interfering with participation or learning? And what support will remove those barriers while building independence? Those questions keep the profile individualized and useful. Planning should include the student, family, teacher, case manager, and relevant specialists.\n\nI will now hand the presentation to Presenter 2, who will begin with Olivia’s strengths and communication.", "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural", "audio": "special-education-A-02.mp3", "words": [{"text": "Category", "start": 0.1, "end": 0.7625, "start_char": 0, "end_char": 8}, {"text": "A", "start": 0.775, "end": 1.1375, "start_char": 9, "end_char": 10}, {"text": "is", "start": 1.15, "end": 1.3875, "start_char": 11, "end_char": 13}, {"text": "Physically", "start": 1.4, "end": 1.875, "start_char": 14, "end_char": 24}, {"text": "Dependent", "start": 1.8875, "end": 2.6625, "start_char": 25, "end_char": 34}, {"text": "The", "start": 3.025, "end": 3.2, "start_char": 36, "end_char": 39}, {"text": "educational", "start": 3.2125, "end": 3.8125, "start_char": 40, "end_char": 51}, {"text